WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.532
- When you put a baby,
and discussion of politics

00:00:02.532 --> 00:00:03.758
together, you're just

00:00:03.758 --> 00:00:04.591
- Oh yeah

00:00:04.591 --> 00:00:05.624
- Guaranteed to not have sleep.

00:00:05.624 --> 00:00:08.207
(upbeat music)

00:00:10.556 --> 00:00:12.835
So today, I'm gonna be
partnered with someone

00:00:12.835 --> 00:00:14.280
who identifies as conservative.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.507
- She happens to be a
liberal, and so we're gonna

00:00:16.507 --> 00:00:19.694
both jointly take care
of a robot baby together.

00:00:19.694 --> 00:00:21.619
I've never held a baby before,

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:23.041
I mean I held it one time maybe.

00:00:23.041 --> 00:00:26.021
- An actual baby toddler?
Yes, but baby? No.

00:00:26.021 --> 00:00:28.604
(upbeat music)

00:00:36.243 --> 00:00:37.463
- [Barrett] I do also know that

00:00:37.463 --> 00:00:38.424
(robot baby cooing)

00:00:38.424 --> 00:00:39.257
- No.

00:00:39.257 --> 00:00:40.765
- Oh no. Should we?

00:00:40.765 --> 00:00:41.598
- [Interviewer] Yes.

00:00:41.598 --> 00:00:42.431
- Okay.

00:00:42.431 --> 00:00:44.738
(robot baby crying)

00:00:44.738 --> 00:00:46.552
You gotta do the bouncy, yeah.

00:00:46.552 --> 00:00:47.699
(robot baby crying)

00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:48.626
- Why are you crying?

00:00:48.626 --> 00:00:50.259
- It's okay. Oh.

00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:51.479
(robot baby stops crying)

00:00:51.479 --> 00:00:52.590
- Oh, that's what it needed.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.861
And that was only like
the first ten seconds.

00:00:54.861 --> 00:00:55.929
- It's stressful, that
was kinda stressful.

00:00:55.929 --> 00:00:57.229
- We're so screwed.

00:00:57.229 --> 00:00:59.628
We will be receiving a
score, a percentage score

00:00:59.628 --> 00:01:02.317
from one to a hundred.
Hopefully we do well.

00:01:02.317 --> 00:01:03.655
Are people gonna think that we're crazy

00:01:03.655 --> 00:01:05.257
for carrying this thing around?

00:01:05.257 --> 00:01:07.385
- Yes, let's embrace it.

00:01:07.385 --> 00:01:09.157
This is the car seat of the future guys.

00:01:09.157 --> 00:01:11.492
- (chuckles) It's not, please
don't ever do this at home.

00:01:11.492 --> 00:01:14.807
I'm gonna see Barrett tonight,
so we will reconnect then.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:15.693
Bye. See ya tonight.

00:01:15.693 --> 00:01:16.711
- Bye, see ya Michael.

00:01:16.711 --> 00:01:18.668
- So I'm gonna have to
go into the grocery store

00:01:18.668 --> 00:01:21.293
with this one here, and
I'm kinda concerned.

00:01:21.293 --> 00:01:23.429
When we were together it was much more fun

00:01:23.429 --> 00:01:24.702
to see everyone else's reactions,

00:01:24.702 --> 00:01:25.535
but then I feel--

00:01:25.535 --> 00:01:26.663
- Alone it's awkward.

00:01:26.663 --> 00:01:28.246
- When I went alone it's
like you just wanna be like,

00:01:28.246 --> 00:01:30.703
just disregard this lump
that's under my shirt.

00:01:30.703 --> 00:01:34.104
(robot baby crying)

00:01:34.104 --> 00:01:35.720
You're crying, at least it's happening now

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.250
and not in the grocery store.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:38.503
Why does it shit so much?

00:01:38.503 --> 00:01:40.920
- Father of the year

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.338
- [Natalie] Oh yeah, what up.

00:01:42.338 --> 00:01:43.259
- We've talked about Trump,

00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:44.514
and I didn't actually vote for Trump.

00:01:44.514 --> 00:01:46.000
- We're about to go on YouTube

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.696
and look at some stuff that he said.

00:01:47.696 --> 00:01:49.278
Makes you tick or what makes you believe--

00:01:49.278 --> 00:01:50.111
- Yeah, but like--

00:01:50.111 --> 00:01:50.944
- In what you believe in?

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.005
- We kinda came around to issues,

00:01:52.005 --> 00:01:53.300
like I'm trying to say something,

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.876
but I don't know quite how to say it yet,

00:01:54.876 --> 00:01:56.110
and then we kept talking and it was like

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:59.501
okay now I kinda know,
once everything filled in.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:02.034
- I started to talk about Gavin McInnes.

00:02:02.034 --> 00:02:05.408
- I do agree with some of
the positions he takes,

00:02:05.408 --> 00:02:06.909
but he's going about it like a dick.

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:09.612
- He thinks he's funny
though, I mean I've adjusted,

00:02:09.612 --> 00:02:10.445
(stammering)

00:02:10.445 --> 00:02:12.423
but I don't agree.

00:02:12.423 --> 00:02:13.914
- I can take the perspective of someone

00:02:13.914 --> 00:02:16.835
that believes otherwise,
and it's like, why would I?

00:02:16.835 --> 00:02:20.029
- Why would I want to if
I were not in agreement?

00:02:20.029 --> 00:02:21.870
- We realized that afterwards,
we have been talking

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.808
for like a solid, 11, 12,
one, two, five straight hours.

00:02:25.808 --> 00:02:28.397
I'm alive, she's alive.

00:02:28.397 --> 00:02:30.559
If he wasn't keeping us up,
we were keeping each other up.

00:02:30.559 --> 00:02:32.609
- Yeah so, it was gonna happen anyways.

00:02:32.609 --> 00:02:35.097
Every time I've had a
conversation with someone

00:02:35.097 --> 00:02:38.618
who doesn't have similar
beliefs, things get really heavy.

00:02:38.618 --> 00:02:42.941
But, I actually left this
conversation, pretty darn happy.

00:02:42.941 --> 00:02:46.524
It's 4:30 a.m. why is
my baby still eating?

00:02:48.784 --> 00:02:53.706
Oh there you go, yeah, ooh
look at that, look at you.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:57.539
Yeah this kid is gonna
go up this entire hill.

00:03:00.662 --> 00:03:02.430
Yeah he's gonna carry him up,

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.851
so I just have to carry my water bottle.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.961
In this situation we found
out yes, we are striving

00:03:06.961 --> 00:03:10.270
towards the same things, we
go about it in a different way

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.607
and I think when we talked about it

00:03:11.607 --> 00:03:13.910
in the context of Michael,
like oh if our child

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:16.168
ended up, growing up, you know as gay.

00:03:16.168 --> 00:03:18.499
So, would it make any difference to you

00:03:18.499 --> 00:03:22.165
if our baby, he grew up
and he came out as gay,

00:03:22.165 --> 00:03:24.083
would that impact you personally?

00:03:24.083 --> 00:03:25.893
- Some people are assholes,
they're gonna do things

00:03:25.893 --> 00:03:28.011
based on what they know.
You can take it personally

00:03:28.011 --> 00:03:29.471
or you can just move on.

00:03:29.471 --> 00:03:30.813
- He never used his tone of voice

00:03:30.813 --> 00:03:34.344
in a way that was
discriminative or put me down,

00:03:34.344 --> 00:03:36.929
and I've been in that
situation many times before.

00:03:36.929 --> 00:03:40.992
So if that didn't occur, I
don't think I would've listened

00:03:40.992 --> 00:03:42.006
I don't think I would've cared.

00:03:42.006 --> 00:03:46.489
If he decided that he wanted
to go and advocate something

00:03:46.489 --> 00:03:49.591
that wasn't what you believed in,

00:03:49.591 --> 00:03:51.504
would you be like, do what you wanna do,

00:03:51.504 --> 00:03:52.766
but I'm not gonna support you.

00:03:52.766 --> 00:03:54.628
- A lot of people do
jump to the conclusion,

00:03:54.628 --> 00:03:58.007
or to certain assumptions,
without enough data.

00:03:58.007 --> 00:03:59.127
And I think that's important for you

00:03:59.127 --> 00:03:59.960
to make you're own decisions.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.546
To speak on the Black Lives Matter thing,

00:04:01.546 --> 00:04:04.255
there are issues that are
still needing to be addressed,

00:04:04.255 --> 00:04:07.014
so those are real and if my son feels,

00:04:07.014 --> 00:04:10.061
and really takes those on as his own,

00:04:10.061 --> 00:04:12.455
I'm for that, at least
he's doing something.

00:04:12.455 --> 00:04:13.709
- [Natalie] (laughs) you literally look

00:04:13.709 --> 00:04:15.081
like your working out with Michael.

00:04:15.081 --> 00:04:16.197
- (chuckles) it's heavy.

00:04:16.197 --> 00:04:20.364
I was mid-shower, and baby
Michael started crying.

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:25.403
- So I guess I'm not
going to just nap anymore.

00:04:25.403 --> 00:04:28.862
Baby is not burping and it's been like,

00:04:28.862 --> 00:04:31.220
straight up 20 minutes. He's so much more

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:33.584
of a mom than I am. I just
thought about single motherhood

00:04:33.584 --> 00:04:34.952
a lot, whenever he was gone.

00:04:34.952 --> 00:04:35.785
(laughing)

00:04:35.785 --> 00:04:37.002
You know if I don't get married

00:04:37.002 --> 00:04:39.005
I'll just adopt a kid, it'll be fine.

00:04:39.005 --> 00:04:39.838
(robot baby crying)

00:04:39.838 --> 00:04:41.007
Can you give me the bottle again?

00:04:41.007 --> 00:04:42.430
- [Barrett] Yeah.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.680
(robot baby stops crying)

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.137
- I fucking hate this baby.

00:04:46.137 --> 00:04:47.307
(both laughing)

00:04:47.307 --> 00:04:49.463
- My beliefs, I'm sticking to my guns,

00:04:49.463 --> 00:04:51.724
in terms of like my conservative views,

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.569
and Natalie is sticking to her guns.

00:04:53.569 --> 00:04:56.200
Through all of that, one,
we were so respectful

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.838
to each other, and I
was able to kind of get

00:04:57.838 --> 00:04:59.511
where she was coming from, as I do think

00:04:59.511 --> 00:05:01.496
that she really did get
where I was coming from.

00:05:01.496 --> 00:05:03.264
- It's kind of amazing having a one-on-one

00:05:03.264 --> 00:05:05.927
time with somebody who
is willing to listen

00:05:05.927 --> 00:05:08.970
and willing to evaluate
your values and beliefs,

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.900
in a non-critical way,
cause I genuinely believe

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:14.479
that politics make up who you are.

00:05:14.479 --> 00:05:17.939
- Talking to her at length,
really made me understand

00:05:17.939 --> 00:05:19.917
the other side a lot more.

00:05:19.917 --> 00:05:21.980
Having something like this
medium, like in a baby

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:24.045
to care for, puts stuff in perspective.

00:05:24.045 --> 00:05:25.594
Like there's policy and there's all these

00:05:25.594 --> 00:05:28.520
different kinds of things,
but when we have something

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:31.012
that's right here, that we
have to take care of together.

00:05:31.012 --> 00:05:34.009
Those things end up being
kind of meaningless in a way.

00:05:34.009 --> 00:05:36.994
- Okay so we're here it's the end.

00:05:36.994 --> 00:05:39.593
It's 10:00 p.m. which means baby is off.

00:05:39.593 --> 00:05:41.305
Which means I can now

00:05:41.305 --> 00:05:43.334
- Stop! Stop! Stop (chuckles) no.

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:44.327
92%!

00:05:44.327 --> 00:05:46.477
- Whoa, we got an A
minus, is that an A minus

00:05:46.477 --> 00:05:47.360
or is that, that's on the verge of A

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.193
- I don't know.

00:05:48.193 --> 00:05:50.401
- We had so many
discussions where our desire

00:05:50.401 --> 00:05:52.870
was really to find a solution, rather than

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:56.096
to continuously butt heads over

00:05:56.096 --> 00:05:57.366
a subject that we don't agree with.

00:05:57.366 --> 00:05:59.959
- Whether I may not
agree with it right now,

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:02.598
through more conversation, you never know.

00:06:02.598 --> 00:06:04.371
Like, you have to be at least open,

00:06:04.371 --> 00:06:07.570
and not closed-minded to
accept some other way to do it.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.718
It is all about common
understanding, and empathy,

00:06:09.718 --> 00:06:11.308
you're being able to kind of see it

00:06:11.308 --> 00:06:13.021
from the other sides perspective.

00:06:13.021 --> 00:06:15.055
I do think if that stuff is in place,

00:06:15.055 --> 00:06:16.080
it does actually work out.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.914
- It's kind of nice to
be able to prove that,

00:06:17.914 --> 00:06:20.114
and tell people that, what the media says,

00:06:20.114 --> 00:06:22.257
about the two different groups or whatever

00:06:22.257 --> 00:06:25.147
sides that there are, it
may not necessarily be true.

00:06:25.147 --> 00:06:25.980
- Yeah.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:27.571
- That's what I felt like
this project did for me

00:06:27.571 --> 00:06:28.972
or for us. Can I do it?

00:06:28.972 --> 00:06:29.805
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:29.805 --> 00:06:30.638
- [Interviewer] Okay.

00:06:30.638 --> 00:06:32.888
(laughing)

00:06:34.367 --> 00:06:35.200
say goodbye.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.033
- He's so sad.

00:06:36.033 --> 00:06:39.033
(robot baby crying)

00:06:41.697 --> 00:06:42.873
I don't think it's working.

00:06:42.873 --> 00:06:45.858
- [Barrett] No, just keep patting him.

